  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14190611/assets/7fb1f147410c9bbcc697813052add5be5a8e2793a7f473e847f7bade2bee504e.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on the interval $[-1,5].$ The graph of $y={f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. It consists  of two line segments and the arc of the semicircle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find $f(4)$ if $f(-1)=2\\pi .$",
